Title:
The Goodmans Kernel

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
GoodmansKernel is a signed Windows WDM kernel driver that embeds the wasm3 interpreter to load and run unsigned WebAssembly (`.wasm`) modules as “kernel payloads.” It aims to provide a modular, iterative way to develop and deploy kernel logic (C/Rust compiled to `wasm32`) while remaining HVCI-compatible by avoiding JIT and W^X violations. The driver exposes an FFI layer that can call arbitrary `ntoskrnl`/`hal` exports by name, plus a set of host imports for memory access, MSR/CPUID/TSC, physical memory, and callback registration. It includes a per-module capability manifest, resource controls (KMUTEX per slot, pool budgets), and safety wrappers like SEH-guarded kernel VA read/write. The project also integrates InfinityHook for trampolining and provides both CLI and a Qt6 GUI for module management, tracing, and logging. It’s primarily useful for red teams, kernel researchers, and tool developers who want a flexible kernel experimentation platform without repeatedly rebuilding/signing new drivers.

Technical Focus:
- Windows kernel WDM driver hosting a WebAssembly runtime (wasm3)
- Kernel FFI to `ntoskrnl.exe` / `hal.dll` exports by name
- IOCTL-based module lifecycle (load/call/unload) and telemetry rings (trace/log)
- Capability-based permission model for guest modules
- InfinityHook-based trampolines and process/image notify callbacks
- HVCI/VBS constraints (no JIT, W^X compliance)

Use Cases:
- Rapid prototyping of kernel-mode logic as swappable `.wasm` modules
- Building modular kernel instrumentation (process/image notifications, tracing)
- Kernel research experiments (MSR/CPUID/TSC access, physmem read/write) under controlled capabilities
- Developing and testing kernel payloads without re-signing a new driver each iteration
- Creating operator tooling (GUI/CLI) for loading, invoking, and monitoring kernel modules

Keywords:
Windows kernel, WDM driver, wasm3, WebAssembly, wasm32, HVCI, VBS, IOCTL, ntoskrnl exports, hal exports, FFI, InfinityHook, trampoline, PsSetCreateProcessNotifyRoutine, image load notify, KMUTEX, SEH, kernel memory read/write, MSR, physical memory, Qt6 GUI